From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: use @vscodium forks of vsce and vsce-sign

Point extension packaging and signature verification at VSCodium's own `@vscodium/vsce` and `@vscodium/vsce-sign` forks instead of Microsoft's `@vscode/*` packages across the moduleignore, gulp package task, extension build lib, manifests, and the signature verification service. Upstream `@vscode/vsce-sign` ships as a proprietary prebuilt binary ("SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE.txt"), and the `@vscodium/vsce` fork drops it as a dependency in favor of the open replacement.

